# Сховані — project rules

## Sources of truth
- Product behavior, copy, flow and animation spec: `docs/app-spec.md`.
- Artwork data, tour stops, touch zones, AI chat rules, sources, museums, journey order: `data/artworks.json` (generated from `docs/artwork-passports.md`, which stays the human-readable reference). Never retype or paraphrase content from these files.
- Visual design: Figma file `YwA6vCDB79wBlD1A8E8Nt0` («хакатон»), section «основні екрани» (node `42:1719`), components page (node `59:2`). Use Figma MCP; inspect the relevant frame before building a screen.
- Technical decisions: the existing code in `web/`.
- If the spec and Figma disagree on behavior, follow `docs/app-spec.md`. If they disagree on visuals, follow Figma.

## Stack
- Next.js (App Router) + TypeScript (strict) + Tailwind CSS + Framer Motion. App lives in `web/`.
- MVP: NO registration, NO auth, NO backend database, NO push. A fake signed-in demo user lives in `web/src/data/demo-user.ts`; progress is stored in localStorage. OpenAI API (server route) for the guide chat.
- The AI guide (tour, touch zones, chat) is the core feature: it gets the highest fidelity and polish.
- Do not add other dependencies without explaining why in your summary.

## Product rules
- Mobile-only PWA. Design frame 390×844, side padding 24px, 4/8 grid, Manrope (via `next/font`). One warm dark theme.
- On desktop, render the app centered at max-width 430px; do not design a desktop layout.
- Figma frames are 390×844, but real viewports are often 667–760px tall (Safari toolbars). Never place screen content with absolute y values from Figma. Anchor top content to the top (with safe area) and bottom sheets/cards to the bottom; images and illustrations fill the remaining space and must not be covered by bottom UI. Check every screen at 390×844, 390×740 and 375×667.
- Use prepared, composed images from Figma (exported renders of frames/groups) instead of re-assembling them from separate raster layers; Figma layers often rely on in-layer crops, masks and blend modes that are lost when exported one by one.
- All UI copy is Ukrainian and comes from the spec/Figma. Never invent copy; if a string is missing, add a `// TODO(copy)` and use the closest existing string.
- The journey only moves forward. No back button inside a path (map → museum → hall → tour).
- Safety: never state or guess where evacuated artworks are stored. Only «твір в укритті».
- Every fact shown to users must come from `docs/artwork-passports.md`. Sources must be real links from the passport.

## Design tokens
- Use Figma variables (names like `bg/screen`, `text/secondary`, `status/stolen-*`) mapped to CSS variables + Tailwind theme. Never hardcode hex values in components.

## Motion
- Use the durations/easings from the animation table in `docs/app-spec.md` (section 8). Keep them in one `motion.ts` constants file.
- Default spring: stiffness 300, damping 30.
- Respect `prefers-reduced-motion`: flights, zooms and lens become 200ms crossfades; pulses are disabled.

## Code conventions
- Small focused components in `web/src/components/<area>/`. Screens in `web/src/app/`.
- Typed data in `web/src/data/`. No content strings hardcoded inside logic.
- Client state: React context + `localStorage`, seeded from the demo user. No Supabase.
- Accessibility: semantic buttons/links, visible focus, accessible names on icon buttons, touch targets ≥ 44px, no info by color alone.
- Secrets only in env vars (`.env.local`, never committed). Provide `.env.example`.

## Working style
- Inspect relevant files and the Figma frame before editing. Make the smallest change that fulfills the stage.
- Do not rewrite files outside the current stage unless required; say why if you do.
- After each stage run `npm run lint`, `npx tsc --noEmit` and `npm run build` in `web/`, fix errors, then summarize: files changed, what works, what to verify manually, open TODOs.
